\begin_layout Standard
In the Mountain car problem, a car is supposed to drive up a mountain that
 is too steep for the car's engine as fast as possible 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "mountaincarOriginal"
literal "true"

\end_inset

.
 To reach the target, an agent has to learn to use the counter slope to
 take a swing.
 The state space is implemented in an unusual way (
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "img:mountaincar-overview"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"

\end_inset

) and could be normalized.
 However, to ensure a natural view on the expert's algorithm, we assume
 that the expert did not normalize the values in his program and uses raw
 values.
